[size=5][b]FFW Scoreboard[/b][/size]
An in-game scoreboard for Far Far West. See what everyone did in a mission: damage, kills, healing, deaths, loadout and jokers, in a panel styled like the game's own menus. Every finished game is saved, so you can look back at it later.

It works the same whether you host or join, and [b]the other players do not need the mod[/b].

[line]
[size=4][b]Disclaimer[/b][/size]
This mod was made entirely by the use of AI.
I have worked with PowerShell, C# and DevOps (CI/CD) in a professional capacity, but never C++ nor Lua.
"Elite dmg"-tracking has not been verified as I do not play Nightmare difficulty.

[line]
[size=4][b]Features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Overview per player:[/b] Kills, Damage, Boss damage, Elite damage, Damage taken, Deaths, Revives, Self heal, Team heal, Shield generated and Friendly fire. The best value in each column is highlighted.
[*][b]Damage types:[/b] Primary and Secondary weapon, Spells split by element (e.g. Cactus, Fire), and the elemental effects Fire, Acid and Elec.
[*][b]Enemies:[/b] damage and kills per enemy type. Bosses such as the Cryptic Train and the Halloween boss get their own line.
[*][b]Loadout:[/b] hero jokers, primary and secondary weapon (with your own weapon jokers), utility, spells, and the jokers picked up during the mission, coloured by rarity.
[*][b]Saved games:[/b] map, difficulty, date, length and Victory / Defeat. Browse them any time, also from the lobby / saloon.
[*]Fixed text size; the board scrolls when it is taller than the screen.
[/list]

[line]
[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/farfarwest/mods/2]UE4SS[/url] installed for Far Far West
[/list]

[size=4][b]Install[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Install UE4SS into [i]...\steamapps\common\FarFarWest\FarFarWest\Binaries\Win64\[/i]
[*]Extract the zip into [i]...\Binaries\Win64\ue4ss\Mods\[/i], so you get [i]Mods\FFW_Scoreboard\[/i] with [i]enabled.txt[/i] and the [i]Scripts[/i] folder inside.
[*]Start the game and press [b]F6[/b] during a mission.
[/list]
[b]Updating:[/b] replace the folder. You can keep your own [i]Scripts\config.lua[/i]; it only holds your settings. Saved games are kept.
[b]Uninstall:[/b] delete the [i]FFW_Scoreboard[/i] folder.

[line]
[size=4][b]Keys[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]F6[/b] - live scoreboard on / off
[*][b]F8[/b] - saved games on / off ([b]Right / Left[/b] = older / newer game)
[*][b]Up / Down[/b] - scroll the board
[*][b]F10[/b] - save the current game now and start a new one
[*][b]F11[/b] - reset the current numbers without saving (handy on the training dummy)
[/list]
All keys can be changed in [i]Scripts\config.lua[/i].

[line]
[size=4][b]Limitations[/b][/size]
Most numbers are the same for everyone in the game. These are not:
[list]
[*][b]Cryptic Train boss: teammates' damage is only tracked when you host.[/b] The train's carriages only report hits to the player who fired and to the host. When you join someone else's game, you see your own train damage, and your teammates show 0 boss damage for the train.
[*][b]Friendly fire:[/b] as host you see everyone's; when you join you mainly see your own.
[*][b]Weakspot hits and missed shots are not tracked[/b] - the game does not send them to every player.
[*][b]Weapon jokers are shown for yourself only[/b] - they are stored in each player's own save.
[*][b]Picked-up jokers[/b] of other players may not show when you join someone else's game.
[*]If you join mid-game, kills, deaths, revives and heals are the totals for the whole game.
[/list]

[size=4][b]After a game update[/b][/size]
New enemies show up as "Other" until the mod knows them. You can name them yourself in [i]config.lua[/i] without waiting for an update:
[code]C.extraEnemyTypes = { { "Scarecrow", "Scarecrow" } }   -- name on the board, part of the class name
C.extraBossPatterns = { "Scarecrow_Boss" }             -- also count it as boss damage[/code]
The class name is written to [i]Scripts\scoreboard.log[/i] ("enemy class counted as 'Other': ...").

[line]
[size=4][b]Bugs and source[/b][/size]
Source code, changelog and issue tracker: [url=https://github.com/Guldfisken/FFW_Scoreboard]github.com/Guldfisken/FFW_Scoreboard[/url]
When reporting a problem, please attach [i]Scripts\scoreboard.log[/i] (and [i]ue4ss\UE4SS.log[/i] if the game crashed).

